# Terra-Cogitia - deployment secrets template.
#
# Copy to:
#   secrets.local.env  -> used by deploy-local.ps1  (REQUIRED; create once, then copy the
#                         SAME file to every machine: it is git-ignored, a clone never brings it)
#   secrets.prod.env   -> used by deploy-all.ps1    (REQUIRED, create it by hand)
#
# These files are git-ignored and never leave this machine except as
# chmod-600 files in <deploy_dir>/secrets/ on the server.
# Format: KEY=value (no quotes needed; single quotes and line breaks are not allowed).
#
# SSH: key-based auth is used when available. Otherwise the scripts read the
# password from the COGITIA_SSH_PASSWORD environment variable, or prompt for it.

# PostgreSQL superuser password for Cogitia-Database (required).
# WARNING: only applied when the database volume is first created. Changing it
# later requires ALTER USER inside the database (see README, Troubleshooting).
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# Mistral API key used by the Back-End AI features (required in production).
MISTRAL_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides
# MISTRAL_MODEL=open-mistral-nemo
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Secret signing the API access tokens and the media file links (Back-End and Worker).
# Strongly recommended in production: without it, a random secret is drawn at each start and
# every user must sign in again after a restart. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# AUTH_SECRET=

# Free media banks (Creation Studio, Search tab). Openverse and Wikimedia Commons work without a key.
# Pexels needs a free API key (https://www.pexels.com/api/); without it, Pexels is simply disabled.
# An Openverse OAuth token raises Openverse's anonymous rate limit.
# PEXELS_API_KEY=
# OPENVERSE_TOKEN=

# Optional shared token between the Back-End and Cogitia-Models (Laya, Whisper).
# Cogitia-Models is reachable only on NetCogitia; the token adds defence in depth.
# MODELS_API_TOKEN=
